{
  "_comment": [
    "Plural category per (locale, type, n) for a numeric argument; every port MUST reproduce each row from its platform library (no hand-written rules). `type` is cardinal or ordinal. `n` is a decimal string with no visible trailing zeros, so the CLDR operands v and f are 0 and a row does not depend on how a port parses numbers (compact exponents are out of scope).",
    "Source: CLDR supplemental plurals.xml and ordinals.xml. Expected values computed with ICU 79.1 / CLDR 49 (ECMAScript Intl.PluralRules) and cross-checked with PHP ext-intl MessageFormatter on ICU 79.1; rule text compared across the CLDR 47, 48 and 49 releases of cldr-json (cldr-core/supplemental/plurals.json, ordinals.json).",
    "`since`: first CLDR major in which the row holds. A port on an older CLDR (47 is the minimum) skips rows whose `since` exceeds its CLDR version; a port on that version or later MUST pass them. Rows without `since` hold from CLDR 47 on.",
    "Coverage: en cardinal one/other, en ordinal one/two/few/other, cy zero/one/two/few/many/other, fr and es many at 1000000, ru/pl/ar few/many/zero, ja other only."
  ],
